// stdlib/darwin_pbpk/circ28_ontology.sio
//
// Drug - enzyme - transporter knowledge base for the circ28 drug layer, closed
// with the WIDE EL+ reasoner of stdlib/ontology/elplus.sio (elplus_wide_*:
// 256 concepts, 16 roles, 32 chains). The pharmacokinetic interaction pairs
// (perpetrator raises / lowers the exposure of victim) are DERIVED from stated
// axioms through role chains; no pair is written down. One closure holds both
// directions.
//
// Every stated axiom has a source that was opened when the axiom was written
// (FDA table of substrates, inhibitors and inducers; DailyMed prescribing
// information; PubMed). The axiom list with URL / PMID and the supporting
// phrase is docs/evidence/CIRC28_ONTOLOGY_AXIOM_SOURCES.md (axiom numbers A1..
// and P1.. below are the numbers of that file).
//
// Claims made: the closure follows the stated axioms (elplus.sio, formal/
// OntologyELPlusClosureComplete.lean). Claims not made: no magnitude (no AUC
// ratio), no dose, no time course, no completeness (only major routes that were
// sourced are stated; minor pathways, weak inhibitors and interactions among the
// perpetrators are left out), no clinical advice. A derived pair is a POTENTIAL
// pharmacokinetic interaction of the class the FDA labels warn about; the
// quantitative lane is stdlib/darwin_pbpk/ddi/.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Encoding (EL+ has no inverse roles, so the direction is fixed like this)
//
//   route  <= exists clears.Victim          "the enzyme / transporter is a major
//                                            route of elimination of the victim"
//   perp   <= exists inhibits_strong.route  (strong index inhibitor, FDA)
//   perp   <= exists inhibits_moderate.route
//   perp   <= exists induces_strong.route
//   perp   <= exists induces_moderate.route
//   victim <= ProteolyticallyCleared | RenallyCleared    (non-enzymatic routes,
//                                            stated as drug classes)
//
//   inhibits_strong   o clears  <=  raises
//   inhibits_moderate o clears  <=  raises
//   induces_strong    o clears  <=  lowers
//   induces_moderate  o clears  <=  lowers
//
// so the derived edge (raises, perp, victim) points from the perpetrator to the
// victim and the route is the middle of the chain. The reasoner only creates a
// derived edge when `exists raises.victim` is interned, so all 15 victims get a
// raises and a lowers existential (also the four that no route reaches: their
// empty answer is the reasoner's, not a missing slot).
//
// Budget (wide limits 256 concepts / 16 roles / 32 chains):
//   concepts 83: 0..22 drugs (study 0..14, perpetrators 15..22), 23 CYP3A4,
//     24 CYP2D6, 25 CYP1A2, 26 CYP2C19, 27 UGT1A4, 28 P-gp, 29 Proteolytically-
//     Cleared, 30 RenallyCleared, 31 top, then existentials: 32..42 clears.victim
//     (11), 43..47 inhibits_strong.route (5), 48 inhibits_moderate.CYP3A4,
//     49..51 induces_strong.route (3), 52 induces_moderate.CYP1A2,
//     53..67 raises.victim (15), 68..82 lowers.victim (15).
//   roles 7: 0 clears, 1 inhibits_strong, 2 inhibits_moderate, 3 induces_strong,
//     4 induces_moderate, 5 raises, 6 lowers.
//   chains 4. Not stated: drug / inhibitor classes, a derived strength, CYP2C9.
//
// Compiler rules this module follows (committed Madaros prebuilt): all state is a
// LOCAL array owned by the caller (the role cube `r`, 1048576 cells) or by one
// function (S, pack, chains) and passed down; no module-level mutable array, no
// named constant used as an array stride (literals), every status of the wide
// entry points is checked. circ28_onto_init* return the number of fixpoint
// rounds (>= 1) or a NEGATIVE refusal code:
//   -1 elplus_wide_role_closure, -2 elplus_wide_seed, -3 elplus_wide_set_concept,
//   -4 elplus_wide_set_exid, -5 elplus_wide_set_chain,
//   -100 - s  elplus_wide_fixpoint_packed refused with status -s (s = 1..8).
//
// Public ids. Drugs 1..23 (study drugs 1..15 in the order of the task, then the
// perpetrators 16..23). Enzymes for the DDI engine: 1 CYP3A4, 2 CYP2D6,
// 3 CYP1A2, 4 CYP2C19, 5 CYP2C9, 6 UGT, 7 other. P-gp is "7 other".
//
// Usage: var r: [bool; 1048576] = [false; 1048576]
//        let rounds = circ28_onto_init(&! r)       (> 0 or refused)
//        circ28_onto_raises(&r, perp_id, victim_id)

use ontology::elplus::{
    elplus_wide_role_closure, elplus_wide_seed, elplus_wide_set_concept,
    elplus_wide_set_exid, elplus_wide_set_chain, elplus_wide_fixpoint_packed,
    elplus_wide_edge
}

